1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
It's Neferpitou.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[both gasp]

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
That is the name
the Queen bestowed upon me.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
From now on, you can call me Neferpitou.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
[opening theme music playing]

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,000
[singer singing in English]

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
LIGHT X AND X DARK

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
[Peggy] Attention squadron leaders
and officers.

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Attention squadron leaders and officers.

14
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Commander Neferpitou will be holding
a conferment ceremony in hall one

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and, of course, you're all invited.

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
[laughs, knuckles cracking]

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
[Peggy] A brief moment of suffering,

18
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
the Chimera Ant nest
is almost certainly up ahead.

19
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Man, that's amazing.

20
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
He tracked him this whole time
and never lost them once.

21
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
He said that his En covers
a radius of 45 meters.

22
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,000
I've heard that the ones called
Nen masters can handle around 50 meters.

23
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Stronger than a master, huh?

24
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
He must be the real deal, I guess.

25
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Yeah, he's the first pro we've met.
Well, at least like this.

26
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
but we really only knew him
as another player in a game.

27
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
And Bisky was an incredible hunter,
but to us…

28
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[Killua] And then there was
the first person to teach us about Nen.

29
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
[Gon] Master Wing,
our Nen master and savior.

30
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
And now that I think about it,

31
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
we always meet people
when we need them the most.

32
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:49,000
It's them, all these people we've met,
who have made us stronger.

33
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
-I guess Razor counts too, huh?
-Yeah.

34
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
It's pretty obvious to me that Ging really
did create Greed Island to train you.

35
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:22,000
I don't know if Ging could have predicted
what was gonna happen when we met Kite,

36
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,000
And he definitely knew you'd follow him,
that much I'm sure of.

37
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
You might be right but this is
a pretty brutal place for training.

38
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,000
And that is exactly the reason why
I keep asking you if your resolve is firm.

39
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,000
[both gasp]

40
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
[Kite] I agree that, like you mentioned,

41
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Ging probably did have
certain expectations

42
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
when he sent you here to meet with me.

43
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
That being said,

44
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
I have no intention of training
the two of you during this journey.

45
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
I only brought you along
because I thought you might be useful.

46
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
From here on,
it all comes down to your resolve.

47
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:28,000
If it's strong, you'll develop your Nen
and improve through combat.

48
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
We're professional hunters, after all.

49
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:41,000
And as you're aware,

50
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
those who call themselves hunters
must get their prey.

51
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
[both gasp]

52
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
For those of our profession,
that's the first commandment.

53
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
We stay on the hunt no matter what.

54
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
It's a battle of resolve.

55
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
and this often means the loser's death.

56
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Improving your Nen is important, sure,

57
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
but to be a successful hunter,

58
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:25,000
you must understand your enemy
as well as yourself.

59
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Wait, I get it.

60
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
That must be why you hit me
when I met you a long time ago, right?

61
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:53,000
If you see that mark then you stay away,
even the animals know that much.

62
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
[gasps softly]

63
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
That was the rule of the forest, it was,
wasn't it?

64
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
You were teaching me the rules
in Ging's place.

65
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[Kite] Oh, that's right,
I just remembered.

66
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:26,000
-It's a hunter's license.
-But whose?

67
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,000
[Kite] It's Ging's.

68
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Huh? It's Ging's?

69
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Just think back to my final test.
Remember what it was?

70
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
He told me I was supposed to use it
to find him someday.

71
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
No, I'd actually forgotten I had it.

72
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
[boys gasp]

73
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Gon, you said you were gonna find Ging
on your own, didn't you?

74
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
Uh…

75
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
[grunts softly]

76
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Then you have to do
what you said you would.

77
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Once I'm done,
I'll find Ging and give this back to him.

78
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,000
We don't wanna lose the trail.

79
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
[Rammot grunts]

80
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[Kite] A monster!

81
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
What is this? I don't believe it.

82
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
[Gon] What's wrong, Kite?

83
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
-[Kite] Gon, Killua, run.
-[boys] Huh?

84
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
I said, go! Get out of here right now!

85
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
I found you.

86
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Get away!

87
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
[both gasp]

88
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[both grunting]

89
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[breath trembling]

90
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,000
[yelling]

91
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[Kite] Idiot!

92
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,000
[soft thud]

93
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Wise decision, Killua.

94
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Now take Gon and get out of here.

95
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[cackling] You're in for it now,
you know that?

96
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:35,000
[Killua] We were too complacent
and overconfident.

97
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
[imperceptible]

98
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
[Killua] We were both worth
less than a one-armed Kite,

99
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
that was his assessment.

100
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
That's the reality.

101
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:59,000
If Kite had been alone,
this probably wouldn't have happened.

102
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
[grunts]

103
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Damn it, we were fools.

104
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,000
Hey.

105
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Is that…

106
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
[panting]

107
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
[breathing heavily]

108
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[dialing]

109
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,000
[line ringing]

110
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Hey, what the hell
do you think you're doing?

111
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
And we're bringing reinforcements.

112
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
-[vehicle approaching]
-Huh?

113
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[gasps]

114
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
[Killua] Chairman Netero.

115
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
What the hell is this? They're just kids.

116
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:29,000
You got burned real bad because
you thought this was gonna be a game.

117
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
That isn't very nice.

118
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:57,000
So, was your adversary that formidable?

119
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
One of them could use Nen.

120
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Of all the aura I've encountered,
this one was the worst.

121
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
You guys are unbelievably strong.

122
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
And still, I don't think
even you could take him.

123
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:49,000
[scoffs] People overrate things
that they can't understand,

124
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,000
We'll take it from here.
You just go to bed and get some rest.

125
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[laughing]

126
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:08,000
How was that just now different
from what I said? Come on, Knov.

127
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
[Knov scoffs]

128
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
well, it just shows
you're missing the whole point.

129
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
In most cases, you don't know
what your opponent's abilities are.

130
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:27,000
And when you're in a fight like that,

131
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,000
All of a sudden,

132
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:37,000
having more or less aura
than the other guy

133
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
isn't really much of an excuse.

134
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Plus, the battle can turn quickly
and at any time.

135
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
That's the essence of Nen combat.

136
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Still, no matter what,

137
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,000
You're worse than a loser.

138
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:15,000
No, he's not. He tried to attack,
so I used force to stop him.

139
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
I didn't have time to hold back,
so I don't know when he'll wake up.

140
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,000
[laughs]

141
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Sounds like the other kid's got
a lot more of a future.

142
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Yet it seems to be true,

143
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
and therefore, we must attempt
to keep the casualties to a minimum.

144
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
If we send in fighters
who aren't strong enough,

145
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[Netero] We have already placed
two assassins in the nearest city.

146
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:30,000
take them down and come find us.

147
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
We don't need just any help…

148
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
only the strong.

149
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,000
WILL YOU FIGHT OR NOT?

150
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
You're worse than a loser.

151
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Well, because you knocked me out.
It was you, right?

152
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:01,000
I mean, if I'd lost control back there,
I would have gotten in the way.

153
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:07,000
And if I had,
all three of us would have died.

154
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,000
-Kite is still alive.
-[gasps]

155
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,000
He would never be beaten,
not by something like that.

156
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
just trying to move is pretty hard on him,
so he's hiding.

157
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:41,000
So now, we get strong and we find him.

158
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
We're gonna go save Kite.

159
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
-Let's go.
-[bird tweeting]

160
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
[Killua] We've gotta get stronger.

161
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:48,000
[Colt] Prepare a freezing chamber
in the fortress.

162
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Make it large enough to store
more than a hundred humans.

163
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
[Neferpitou] To ensure that
my collection doesn't rot.

164
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,000
[upbeat music playing]

165
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
[Gon] Next time, Promise and Reunion.

166
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Gon snores]

167
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:39,000
It just has to be Killua.

168
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,000
[Killua] Yeah, okay. Just stay asleep.
